<title>USA: Theragenics sells shares to J&amp;J.</title>
<headline>Theragenics sells shares to J&amp;J.</headline>
<dateline>NORCROSS, Ga. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Theragenics Corp said on Monday that Johnson &amp; Johnson has acquired 254,453 shares of Theragenics common stock through a private placement for a total purchase price of $5.0 million.</p>
<p>Theragenics also said that it has signed a definitive agreement with Indigo Medical Inc, a unit of Johnson &amp; Johnson, granting Indigo exclusive worldwide rights to market and sell its TheraSeed for use in the treatment of prostate cancer.</p>
</text>
